      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/who-iris/v0/ns/glossary/hrhis-registry-2015",
      "@type": "skos:ConceptScheme",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Human resources for health information system: minimum data set for health workforce registry (2015) — system functional requirements",
      "skos:definition": "System types and functional requirements from the WHO guide 'Human resources for health information system: minimum data set for health workforce registry' (2015, ISBN 9789241549226), held in this library as 9789241549226-eng. Owner, 2026-11-01: an inspirational, non-definitional reference for the DTH-HRH handbook's Chapter 7 (Functional Requirements); these concepts contribute to a definition and are not definitional, so no term carries skos:definition. Three kinds of concept: system types (Figure 3: the health information system, its sub-systems, the HRH information system and its functional components, among them the health workforce registry); the four functional domains (Figure 4, Table 1) and Table 2's information categories; and one concept per functional-requirement block of library/9789241549226-eng, broader-linked to the system type it is stated for and related to its domain or category. Labels are the source's own words; a requirement the source gives no name is labelled with its full statement. Owner, 2026-11-12: the minimum data set is cross-referenced from DTH-HRH, though it is not the basis of the handbook's core data elements, so Table 3's ten data sets and the nineteen data-element sheets are added as non-definitional concepts under 'minimum-data-set' (Tables 6-7 are not represented). Every term is a candidate until a person confirms it.",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "2026-11-12",
      "dcterms:modified": "2026-11-12",
      "dcterms:source": "library/9789241549226-eng/",
      "dcterms:license": "LicenseRef-WHO-All-Rights-Reserved"
    },
